cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalisation in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "Hyperbolic and Dispersive 1D PDE in Lean 4: Weak Solutions, Shock Waves, Gradient Blow-up, and Solitons"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-28
authors:
  - family-names: Izquierdo Perez
    given-names: Bezalel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5993-4057"
    alias: Alektronnik
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alektronnik/M4TH"
url: "https://github.com/Alektronnik/M4TH"
abstract: >
  Self-contained formalisation in Lean 4 over Mathlib of the elementary theory
  of one-dimensional evolutionary PDE of hyperbolic and dispersive type. Three
  independent packages: ConservationLaws (weak solutions, travelling shocks,
  Rankine-Hugoniot, Lax entropy condition for arbitrary flux), BurgersBlowUp
  (finite-time gradient blow-up via exact Riccati solution), and KdV (exact
  one-soliton profile and conservation laws). Zero axioms, zero sorry. Every
  headline theorem carries the clean axiom certificate [propext,
  Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. First formalisation of weak solutions of
  conservation laws, Rankine-Hugoniot, Lax entropy, gradient blow-up for a
  nonlinear PDE, and the KdV soliton, in any major proof assistant.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - partial differential equations
  - conservation laws
  - Rankine-Hugoniot
  - Lax entropy condition
  - Burgers equation
  - gradient blow-up
  - KdV equation
  - solitons
  - weak solutions
  - shock waves
